{
  "id": "alcohol-withdrawal-delirium",
  "term": "Alcohol Withdrawal Delirium",
  "definition": "Alcohol withdrawal delirium is a sudden severe mental disturbance that can happen when a person who has been drinking alcohol heavily over time stops or sharply reduces use. It commonly involves confusion, delusions, vivid hallucinations, tremor, agitation, insomnia, and overactivation of the body's automatic functions such as fast heart rate, high blood pressure, sweating, and enlarged pupils; it was formerly called delirium tremens.",
